00:00:00,010 --> 00:01:33,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:42,000
Brother Qi tells me to recount every daily event,

2
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:42,640
every word spoken,

3
00:01:42,640 --> 00:01:43,239
every person met,

4
00:01:43,239 --> 00:01:45,359
and every action taken.

5
00:01:45,359 --> 00:01:46,359
He checks every day.

6
00:01:46,359 --> 00:01:48,200
If I mess up again, he won't take me along.

7
00:01:50,799 --> 00:01:52,200
He only knows how to demand things of others.

8
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:53,480
Can he even remember all that himself?

9
00:01:54,040 --> 00:01:54,920
He really can.

10
00:01:55,359 --> 00:01:56,359
I asked around.

11
00:01:56,359 --> 00:01:58,159
I don't know if he has some trick,

12
00:01:58,159 --> 00:02:00,239
or if some people are just born with a good memory.

13
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:04,239
He made us get up past six to come here.

14
00:02:04,239 --> 00:02:05,599
I thought it was some big operation,

15
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:07,799
but it turns out to be more legwork.

16
00:02:10,039 --> 00:02:11,479
Actually, last time,

17
00:02:11,639 --> 00:02:13,599
I didn't mean to refuse to partner with you.

18
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:15,639
You said you were going to resign.

19
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:17,400
You seemed dead set on leaving.

20
00:02:17,439 --> 00:02:18,800
I just joined this unit.

21
00:02:19,039 --> 00:02:21,080
It felt like everything I asked or said was wrong.

22
00:02:21,159 --> 00:02:24,000
That's why I said I wouldn't partner with you.

23
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:30,560
Your car is sputtering. Will it make it?

24
00:02:30,680 --> 00:02:32,159
I checked it before we left.

25
00:02:32,159 --> 00:02:33,000
It should be fine.

26
00:02:34,479 --> 00:02:35,400
"Should"?

27
00:02:36,039 --> 00:02:37,800
It better not break down halfway.

28
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:39,159
I don't want to help you push it again.

29
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:40,960
Don't jinx it.

30
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:42,000
Don't let the car hear you.

31
00:02:42,159 --> 00:02:43,000
Why?

32
00:02:43,159 --> 00:02:44,520
Jinxes always come true.

33
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:45,560
Brother Qi said so.

34
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:49,080
Superstitious nonsense everywhere.

35
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:51,560
Wake me when we get there.

36
00:02:57,680 --> 00:02:58,439
Hey.

37
00:02:58,439 --> 00:02:59,080
Don't talk.

38
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,080
I was about to pee myself.

39
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:04,919
Don't we have to wait if we go inside anyway?

40
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:06,599
Would the result be any different?

41
00:03:07,719 --> 00:03:09,240
You always talk so much in the bathroom.

42
00:03:09,520 --> 00:03:10,439
Get to the point.

43
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:14,319
What about the people who showed up at the postman's house?

44
00:03:14,319 --> 00:03:16,599
There were about six of them in total.

45
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,039
We did a rough check on them.

46
00:03:20,919 --> 00:03:21,879
Nothing was found.

47
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:23,639
But there's one guy I'm not sure about.

48
00:03:24,639 --> 00:03:25,439
We need to keep looking.

49
00:03:25,439 --> 00:03:26,840
You sure talk a lot for someone who isn't sure.

50
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:27,919
Come back when you've figured it out.

51
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:39,280
Look this way. Look over here!

52
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:46,719
Good.

53
00:03:47,159 --> 00:03:48,000
Stand still!

54
00:03:57,159 --> 00:03:57,599
Freeze!

55
00:03:57,919 --> 00:03:58,360
Stop!

56
00:03:58,840 --> 00:03:59,280
Freeze!

57
00:03:59,719 --> 00:04:00,159
Nobody move!

58
00:04:00,879 --> 00:04:01,319
Stop!

59
00:04:02,319 --> 00:04:02,639
What are you doing?

60
00:04:02,919 --> 00:04:03,199
Freeze!

61
00:04:03,199 --> 00:04:03,800
Police! Don't move!

62
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:04,919
Don't move!

63
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:06,360
Stop!

64
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:07,520
Stop him!

65
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:10,120
Freeze!

66
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:16,879
Should we go catch him?

67
00:04:16,879 --> 00:04:18,519
If they didn't ask, you don't need to go.

68
00:04:18,639 --> 00:04:19,959
Just take your photos.

69
00:04:19,959 --> 00:04:21,079
Getting the evidence is enough.

70
00:04:24,839 --> 00:04:25,319
Stop!

71
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:26,879
Stop right there! Don't run!

72
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:34,240
Stop! Don't move!

73
00:04:36,759 --> 00:04:37,240
Freeze!

74
00:04:38,879 --> 00:04:39,439
Don't move!

75
00:04:39,439 --> 00:04:40,240
Get down!

76
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:41,439
What? I'm just fishing!

77
00:04:41,639 --> 00:04:42,480
I'm not the one taking photos!

78
00:04:42,480 --> 00:04:43,079
Move!

79
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:56,600
Stop!

80
00:05:03,639 --> 00:05:04,199
Stop!

81
00:05:04,720 --> 00:05:05,680
Stop running!

82
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:06,720
It's dangerous ahead!

83
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:34,720
Bro,

84
00:05:34,879 --> 00:05:36,600
we're partners in this.

85
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:38,519
We split the money half and half.

86
00:05:38,519 --> 00:05:39,639
We both get a cut.

87
00:05:40,279 --> 00:05:42,040
If we always use a crappy camera

88
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:43,720
and just make do...

89
00:05:43,839 --> 00:05:44,800
Our costs might be low,

90
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:46,160
but if they don't want your photos,

91
00:05:46,160 --> 00:05:47,319
they won't give you a single cent.

92
00:05:47,319 --> 00:05:48,959
You've said a lot. What do you want?

93
00:05:49,639 --> 00:05:50,399
To take a gamble.

94
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:52,600
I'll return it to you as soon as I'm done.

95
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:53,879
You'd better be careful.

96
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:56,040
Even together, we couldn't pay for it.

97
00:06:02,439 --> 00:06:04,480
I saw him in the post office backyard that day.

98
00:06:05,079 --> 00:06:05,920
Theoretically speaking,

99
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:07,480
his movements were suspicious.

100
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:08,680
But I checked,

101
00:06:08,680 --> 00:06:09,879
and he did have a legitimate reason.

102
00:06:10,120 --> 00:06:11,560
So it's hard to say.

103
00:06:17,319 --> 00:06:18,959
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

104
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:00,639
This way.

105
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:04,480
And over here.

106
00:07:05,279 --> 00:07:06,120
Let's go, let's go.

107
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:08,319
Just take a look around.

108
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:11,879
Wherever you point that golden finger of yours,

109
00:07:12,079 --> 00:07:13,680
I'll get the leaders to approve it for you.

110
00:07:13,680 --> 00:07:15,319
Building factories, building dorms...

111
00:07:15,319 --> 00:07:16,680
You can build whatever you want.

112
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:17,720
The advantage is

113
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:19,000
that costs are low.

114
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,759
A bowl of noodles here in the county

115
00:07:21,079 --> 00:07:22,959
is fifty cents cheaper than in the city.

116
00:07:23,199 --> 00:07:24,439
Labor is the same way.

117
00:07:24,439 --> 00:07:25,279
As for the disadvantage,

118
00:07:25,279 --> 00:07:27,120
it's logistics and transportation.

119
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:28,800
It's always going to burn a bit more gas.

120
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:31,639
You said you'd take me to find my great-aunt,

121
00:07:32,199 --> 00:07:34,160
but we only talk about building factories.

122
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:36,959
I'll leave the math to you, brother.

123
00:07:36,959 --> 00:07:38,399
We have to find your great-aunt,

124
00:07:38,399 --> 00:07:39,759
and look at the land too.

125
00:07:39,839 --> 00:07:41,600
Time is also a cost, you know.

126
00:07:41,720 --> 00:07:44,319
Investing requires careful calculation.

127
00:07:44,399 --> 00:07:46,240
Don't worry about finding your great-aunt.

128
00:07:46,319 --> 00:07:47,519
He used to be a township head.

129
00:07:47,519 --> 00:07:48,279
He'll definitely get it done.

130
00:07:48,279 --> 00:07:48,920
Definitely, definitely.

131
00:07:48,920 --> 00:07:49,600
Right?

132
00:07:50,879 --> 00:07:51,439
Take a guess

133
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:54,480
where he was before the county investment bureau.

134
00:07:55,959 --> 00:07:57,639
He must have been promoted after being township head.

135
00:07:57,639 --> 00:07:58,600
Since he's so capable,

136
00:07:59,279 --> 00:08:01,079
he must have been given a really tough job.

137
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:02,439
Where was it?

138
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:05,240
City Health Bureau Coordination Section.

139
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:07,160
Coordination...

140
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:08,360
That's grueling work.

141
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:09,759
You couldn't do it unless you're Superman.

142
00:08:09,759 --> 00:08:10,879
No, no, no.

143
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:13,120
What do you want for lunch?

144
00:08:15,879 --> 00:08:18,040
Got any fresher seafood?

145
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:18,600
Let's get some.

146
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:19,079
Well...

147
00:08:19,079 --> 00:08:20,199
We'll need to find a boat for that.

148
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:22,040
One that heads out to sea early in the morning.

149
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:24,000
It's probably too late now.

150
00:08:24,319 --> 00:08:27,560
Let's check out the seafood market nearby.

151
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:28,439
Let's go. Get in.

152
00:08:28,439 --> 00:08:28,680
Let's go.

153
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:31,319
Vice Chairman of the CPPCC Wu Xueqian said,

154
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:35,200
the Shimonoseki Treaty was forced on us,

155
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:37,480
and Japan forcibly took Taiwan, China.

156
00:08:37,799 --> 00:08:39,559
The Chinese people must learn from history.

157
00:08:39,799 --> 00:08:41,159
Taiwan, China will return sooner or later.

158
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:42,120
Boss.

159
00:08:42,120 --> 00:08:43,519
Which cigarettes sell the best?

160
00:08:43,799 --> 00:08:44,639
White Peony,

161
00:08:44,639 --> 00:08:45,000
Da Qianmen.

162
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:45,679
They all sell well.

163
00:08:46,559 --> 00:08:48,600
I see some non-local brands.

164
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:49,960
Do out-of-towners buy here too?

165
00:08:50,240 --> 00:08:50,799
Yeah.

166
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,039
Give me a pack of Chunghwa.

167
00:08:53,919 --> 00:08:54,360
Sure.

168
00:08:54,919 --> 00:08:56,360
To know if troops are mobilizing,

169
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:58,720
just check cigarette sales at the local shops.

170
00:08:59,159 --> 00:09:00,320
And two packs of Yunxiao.

171
00:09:00,519 --> 00:09:00,799
How much?

172
00:09:00,799 --> 00:09:01,279
Forty-nine in total.

173
00:09:01,279 --> 00:09:02,679
If non-local cigarettes sell fast,

174
00:09:02,679 --> 00:09:05,039
it means large troop units have moved in.

175
00:09:05,679 --> 00:09:06,720
The matches are free.

176
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:09,799
Boss, boss! Come look at our fish.

177
00:09:09,799 --> 00:09:11,080
Freshly caught today.

178
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:12,039
Three yuan a jin.

179
00:09:12,039 --> 00:09:13,360
The jellyfish is also very fresh.

180
00:09:13,679 --> 00:09:14,480
How much for the jellyfish?

181
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:15,039
Three yuan a jin.

182
00:09:15,039 --> 00:09:15,799
Come on, pick some.

183
00:09:15,799 --> 00:09:16,840
Three yuan? That's so expensive.

184
00:09:17,039 --> 00:09:18,879
If he wants seafood, he should just eat it.

185
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:21,799
Yet he's haggling over jellyfish.

186
00:09:21,799 --> 00:09:23,679
He'd start a fight if he were buying a house.

187
00:09:23,679 --> 00:09:25,279
I know many Taiwan, China businessmen.

188
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:28,120
All they ever talk about is big deals.

189
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:29,440
Selling airplanes today,

190
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:30,679
selling ships tomorrow.

191
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:34,159
Yet they're so stingy over a bowl of shacha noodles.

192
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:35,120
Believe it or not,

193
00:09:35,159 --> 00:09:36,879
if the vinegar cost money,

194
00:09:36,879 --> 00:09:38,399
he wouldn't even dip his crabs in it.

195
00:09:40,639 --> 00:09:42,519
But when spending money on girls,

196
00:09:42,519 --> 00:09:43,840
he wouldn't blink an eye.

197
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:44,960
There are no fakes here!

198
00:09:44,960 --> 00:09:46,240
What are you talking about, man?

199
00:09:46,320 --> 00:09:47,440
Stop arguing, you two.

200
00:09:48,639 --> 00:09:49,759
We made them argue.

201
00:09:49,759 --> 00:09:50,159
Look, look.

202
00:09:51,039 --> 00:09:51,519
We're out of liquor.

203
00:09:51,840 --> 00:09:52,559
I'll go get another bottle.

204
00:09:52,679 --> 00:09:53,519
Let me go get it.

205
00:09:53,519 --> 00:09:54,559
We have to have a good time.

206
00:09:55,039 --> 00:09:55,559
Alright, alright.

207
00:09:55,559 --> 00:09:56,600
No need to get anything too fancy.

208
00:09:56,799 --> 00:09:57,519
Alright.

209
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:02,279
Boss, a bottle of premium sorghum liquor.

210
00:10:02,279 --> 00:10:02,799
Coming right up!

211
00:10:05,919 --> 00:10:06,799
Let me make a call.

212
00:10:06,799 --> 00:10:07,320
Okay.

213
00:10:10,879 --> 00:10:12,720
Boss, check for table 15!

214
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:13,519
Alright, coming!

215
00:10:30,360 --> 00:10:31,600
Is this the county hospital duty room?

216
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:34,480
City Health Bureau Coordination Section.

217
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:35,879
Over the past week to two weeks,

218
00:10:35,879 --> 00:10:37,480
your dampness relief and heatstroke medication,

219
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:38,320
how are they selling?

220
00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:39,240
Have there been big changes?

221
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:40,600
For the duty statistics.

222
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:42,279
I know it's a lot of hard work.

223
00:10:42,559 --> 00:10:43,600
I need specific data.

224
00:10:45,879 --> 00:10:46,600
Okay, got it.

225
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:53,120
ID.

226
00:10:53,519 --> 00:10:54,159
Looking for someone.

227
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:54,879
Who?

228
00:10:54,879 --> 00:10:56,120
He's looking for me. For me.

229
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:57,120
Family member.

230
00:10:57,120 --> 00:10:58,240
Just picking something up and leaving.

231
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:00,600
Okay, come with me to sign in.

232
00:11:03,399 --> 00:11:04,360
One, two!

233
00:11:04,360 --> 00:11:08,120
One, two, three, four!

234
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:11,840
One, two, three, four!

235
00:11:12,080 --> 00:11:13,559
One, two, one!

236
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:15,399
One, two, one!

237
00:11:15,879 --> 00:11:17,519
One, two, one!

238
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:19,799
Hurry up and get the money.

239
00:11:19,799 --> 00:11:20,879
Pay for my camera.

240
00:11:21,360 --> 00:11:22,240
My friend said

241
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:24,039
photos of the military compound

242
00:11:24,399 --> 00:11:25,679
can fetch a much higher price.

243
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:29,320
One, two, three, four!

244
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:33,320
One, two, three, four!

245
00:11:33,320 --> 00:11:35,440
One, two, three, four!

246
00:12:07,039 --> 00:12:08,080
I just went to take a leak.

247
00:12:08,440 --> 00:12:09,960
Last time he came back was just to get a blanket.

248
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:10,960
Hasn't he been back since?

249
00:12:12,399 --> 00:12:14,000
I don't ever want to come back here again.

250
00:12:21,879 --> 00:12:23,320
Let's go out and have some fun, okay?

251
00:12:30,240 --> 00:12:31,000
Let's go.

252
00:12:32,919 --> 00:12:34,519
One, two, one.

253
00:12:35,039 --> 00:12:36,720
One, two, one.

254
00:12:37,879 --> 00:12:38,720
Don't worry.

255
00:12:39,159 --> 00:12:40,879
I'll definitely make a lot of money.

256
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:44,080
I won't let you live such a miserable life anymore.

257
00:12:50,720 --> 00:12:52,840
There must be unusual movements among the troops near Pingtan.

258
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:53,919
How much is this?

259
00:12:53,919 --> 00:12:54,519
Three yuan a jin.

260
00:12:54,519 --> 00:12:55,240
Come, pick some out.

261
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:56,120
Three? That's so expensive.

262
00:12:56,840 --> 00:12:59,240
The stable price of dried shrimp

263
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:00,159
suddenly went up.

264
00:13:00,639 --> 00:13:02,639
Same for stable items like oil, salt,

265
00:13:03,039 --> 00:13:04,080
soy sauce, vinegar, and chilies.

266
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,480
Many corner stores are restocking them.

267
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:06,919
I noticed some aren't local cigarettes.

268
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:08,639
Do out-of-towners buy them here too?

269
00:13:08,639 --> 00:13:09,279
Yeah.

270
00:13:09,279 --> 00:13:10,600
This only proves one thing.

271
00:13:10,919 --> 00:13:13,039
There's a large influx of new troops stationed nearby.

272
00:13:13,440 --> 00:13:14,960
There are too many new mouths to feed in the military canteens.

273
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:15,960
Over the past week or two,

274
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:17,480
how are your dampness and heatstroke pills

275
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:18,399
been selling?

276
00:13:18,399 --> 00:13:19,360
Have there been big changes?

277
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:20,279
Data.

278
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:21,399
I need specific data.

279
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:23,759
The county hospital, the TCM hospital,

280
00:13:23,759 --> 00:13:26,320
and Chengguan Hospital's similar pills

281
00:13:26,480 --> 00:13:28,000
are also selling more than usual.

282
00:13:29,159 --> 00:13:31,879
With non-local smokes and liquor sold out,

283
00:13:32,240 --> 00:13:33,679
it's highly likely that these troops

284
00:13:34,360 --> 00:13:36,759
are Beijing troops unused to humidity.

285
00:13:37,559 --> 00:13:38,759
The news of Lee Teng-hui's "visit" to the U.S.

286
00:13:38,759 --> 00:13:39,879
has already spread.

287
00:13:40,879 --> 00:13:42,320
If I'm not mistaken,

288
00:13:42,600 --> 00:13:43,720
these stationed troops

289
00:13:44,279 --> 00:13:45,600
are also related to the Taiwan Strait.

290
00:13:45,600 --> 00:13:46,200
I've said it several times.

291
00:13:46,480 --> 00:13:48,519
Mail sent from Zhangzhou hasn't arrived for days.

292
00:13:48,720 --> 00:13:49,840
It used to be a

293
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:51,639
postman named Fan delivering it.

294
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,120
I haven't seen him lately.

295
00:13:53,879 --> 00:13:55,000
Did they replace him?

296
00:13:57,120 --> 00:13:57,840
No wonder.

297
00:13:58,679 --> 00:13:59,960
Mainland State Security is closing in.

298
00:14:00,639 --> 00:14:02,039
The postman has also disappeared.

299
00:14:02,279 --> 00:14:04,000
There are unusual movements in many military regions.

300
00:14:04,240 --> 00:14:05,440
Something big is going to happen.

301
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:07,679
Is this Chen Leyuan's home?

302
00:14:07,960 --> 00:14:08,720
My name is Lin.

303
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:09,600
I'm his colleague.

304
00:14:10,559 --> 00:14:10,840
It's me.

305
00:14:10,840 --> 00:14:11,320
Where are you?

306
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:12,720
Don't worry about where I am.

307
00:14:13,039 --> 00:14:14,279
Let me ask you something.

308
00:14:14,279 --> 00:14:16,399
Like, if... if someone quits halfway through,

309
00:14:16,399 --> 00:14:17,240
Right, right, right.

310
00:14:17,240 --> 00:14:18,200
What's the policy?

311
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:18,799
Get injured?

312
00:14:18,799 --> 00:14:19,840
Is an injury the only way?

313
00:14:20,240 --> 00:14:20,759
Yeah.

314
00:14:21,679 --> 00:14:23,279
What if I get sick or something?

315
00:14:23,679 --> 00:14:26,080
Like being unable to sleep every night.

316
00:14:26,879 --> 00:14:27,879
Palpitations and chest tightness.

317
00:14:28,559 --> 00:14:30,120
Do they accept mainland sick notes?

318
00:14:30,120 --> 00:14:30,600
What sick note?

319
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:31,399
Like from a key hospital.

320
00:14:31,399 --> 00:14:31,759
Like, like...

321
00:14:31,759 --> 00:14:34,039
Would they accept a specialist's note from a Grade 3A hospital?

322
00:14:34,039 --> 00:14:35,240
Of course not.

323
00:14:35,240 --> 00:14:36,120
What are you up to?

324
00:14:36,120 --> 00:14:37,279
Alright, alright, got it.

325
00:14:39,279 --> 00:14:41,559
The Tong'an troops were photographed.

326
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:42,399
There's more than one copy.

327
00:14:42,399 --> 00:14:44,440
It involves the missile troops' exercises.

328
00:14:44,440 --> 00:14:45,679
The Director's instruction is

329
00:14:45,679 --> 00:14:48,000
to screen everyone who took photos lately.

330
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:49,279
No wrong arrests, and no one slips away.

331
00:14:49,279 --> 00:14:51,039
Minor offenders will be reprimanded.

332
00:14:51,039 --> 00:14:52,399
Major offenders will be rounded up overnight.

333
00:14:52,399 --> 00:14:54,039
Nobody is sleeping tonight.

334
00:15:23,120 --> 00:15:24,120
What are you doing?

335
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:25,759
I didn't do anything!

336
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:27,679
Hey! I didn't do anything!

337
00:15:27,679 --> 00:15:28,559
I didn't do anything!

338
00:15:28,559 --> 00:15:29,679
What are you doing?

339
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:37,399
This is the room.

340
00:15:49,879 --> 00:15:50,679
Jin Lina.

341
00:15:51,320 --> 00:15:51,960
Lina.

342
00:15:52,879 --> 00:15:53,480
Hey, wake up.

343
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:55,679
Get dressed and come with me.

344
00:15:56,279 --> 00:15:57,559
What's wrong, Ms. Zhao?

345
00:15:57,879 --> 00:15:59,639
Ms. Zhao, it's so late. What's going on?

346
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:01,480
What is it, in the middle of the night?

347
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:02,559
It has nothing to do with any of you.

348
00:16:02,559 --> 00:16:03,840
You have class tomorrow morning.

349
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:04,840
Hurry back to sleep.

350
00:16:07,679 --> 00:16:08,759
And no gossiping.

351
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:15,240
What's going on?

352
00:16:15,399 --> 00:16:17,039
Dragged away in the middle of the night.

353
00:16:17,039 --> 00:16:17,919
Something's definitely up.

354
00:16:17,919 --> 00:16:18,879
She's been acting weird.

355
00:16:18,879 --> 00:16:19,960
Could she be pregnant?

356
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:21,039
No way.

357
00:16:21,679 --> 00:16:22,639
Just go to sleep.

358
00:16:23,759 --> 00:16:25,200
Do you know Lu Zhifei?

359
00:16:30,879 --> 00:16:32,080
What is your relationship with him?

360
00:16:32,679 --> 00:16:35,000
We're from the same hometown, Daizhou.

361
00:16:35,320 --> 00:16:36,440
Just someone from your hometown?

362
00:16:38,639 --> 00:16:39,559
He's also my boyfriend.

363
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:41,399
There's something

364
00:16:41,799 --> 00:16:43,840
we'd like to verify with you right now.

365
00:16:43,919 --> 00:16:45,519
Did something happen to him?

366
00:16:45,519 --> 00:16:48,039
Where were you yesterday afternoon?

367
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:51,960
And where was Lu Zhifei?

368
00:16:55,759 --> 00:16:57,600
Jin Lina. Jin Lina!

369
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:59,279
Just tell us what you know.

370
00:16:59,480 --> 00:17:00,360
Don't be afraid.

371
00:17:02,679 --> 00:17:04,440
He was with me.

372
00:17:04,960 --> 00:17:06,160
In the dorm the whole time.

373
00:17:06,759 --> 00:17:08,359
We didn't go out before dark.

374
00:17:08,559 --> 00:17:10,559
After he helped me move my things,

375
00:17:10,640 --> 00:17:11,559
he didn't leave.

376
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:13,559
The time matches up,

377
00:17:13,960 --> 00:17:14,960
but the location doesn't.

378
00:17:15,440 --> 00:17:17,000
Do you think you can get away with this?

379
00:17:19,039 --> 00:17:20,720
Tell me the truth.

380
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:22,359
Why did you lie?

381
00:17:24,559 --> 00:17:25,440
I didn't.

382
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:29,920
Still playing dumb, huh?

383
00:17:30,240 --> 00:17:31,079
Let me tell you something,

384
00:17:31,279 --> 00:17:33,920
if you come clean today,

385
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:35,839
you can go home tonight.

386
00:17:36,319 --> 00:17:38,759
But if you dare to lie to me again,

387
00:17:39,240 --> 00:17:40,160
three months.

388
00:17:40,799 --> 00:17:41,599
Half a year.

389
00:17:41,599 --> 00:17:42,640
From now on,

390
00:17:44,640 --> 00:17:45,839
you'll be living here.

391
00:17:50,720 --> 00:17:52,519
I'll talk. I'll tell you everything.

392
00:17:52,519 --> 00:17:53,400
I... I really didn't know

393
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:54,880
why they wanted those photos,

394
00:17:54,880 --> 00:17:56,839
but I knew something was off about them.

395
00:17:57,160 --> 00:17:58,160
You knew,

396
00:17:58,160 --> 00:17:59,400
and your buddy knew.

397
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:01,039
You both understood perfectly,

398
00:18:01,039 --> 00:18:03,279
yet you buried your heads in the sand,

399
00:18:03,519 --> 00:18:04,759
pretending you weren't breaking the law.

400
00:18:05,359 --> 00:18:06,160
Did I get that right?

401
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:10,400
Where did you first find the call for submissions?

402
00:18:10,480 --> 00:18:11,640
On a telephone pole.

403
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:13,240
Right by the photo studio.

404
00:18:13,359 --> 00:18:14,960
They were posted everywhere a while back.

405
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:15,960
And the contact info?

406
00:18:15,960 --> 00:18:18,160
We paged them every time.

407
00:18:18,559 --> 00:18:20,440
And we only used public payphones.

408
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:23,160
What about them? Have you met them?

409
00:18:23,160 --> 00:18:24,079
Never seen them.

410
00:18:24,079 --> 00:18:25,319
Not even once.

411
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:26,920
It's definitely a crime.

412
00:18:26,920 --> 00:18:28,880
Fortunately, it didn't cause much harm.

413
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:30,279
Here's the situation now.

414
00:18:30,440 --> 00:18:31,279
It could be a major issue,

415
00:18:31,559 --> 00:18:32,400
or a minor one.

416
00:18:33,079 --> 00:18:35,079
Do it again, and it becomes major.

417
00:18:35,880 --> 00:18:37,279
Don't do it again, and it stays minor.

418
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:39,759
Think carefully about your future path.

419
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:40,680
Tell us where you stand.

420
00:18:41,799 --> 00:18:42,799
I'll never take photos again.

421
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:44,160
I really won't.

422
00:18:44,480 --> 00:18:45,559
How did you do the handover?

423
00:18:46,400 --> 00:18:47,200
Carrier pigeons?

424
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:49,079
After we took the photos,

425
00:18:49,079 --> 00:18:51,319
I'd put them in a small box,

426
00:18:51,480 --> 00:18:54,119
and leave it on the studio's windowsill.

427
00:18:54,119 --> 00:18:57,000
Someone would come take them at night

428
00:18:57,440 --> 00:18:58,400
and leave the money.

429
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:00,680
Did you drop off the photos this time?

430
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:02,160
I didn't get the chance.

431
00:19:02,720 --> 00:19:04,000
I was brought here instead.

432
00:19:44,480 --> 00:19:45,480
Are you trying to kill me?!

433
00:19:46,039 --> 00:19:47,960
I was scared to death driving and waiting!

434
00:19:48,079 --> 00:19:49,160
You were leaning against the window,

435
00:19:49,160 --> 00:19:50,599
you could at least say something.

436
00:19:50,680 --> 00:19:52,480
Did you know a State Security officer

437
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:53,880
who got pranked exactly like this?

438
00:19:54,119 --> 00:19:55,279
He had some kind of heart attack

439
00:19:55,279 --> 00:19:56,839
and died after failing resuscitation?

440
00:19:57,799 --> 00:19:59,440
It was just a joke.

441
00:19:59,759 --> 00:20:01,039
Why are you so tense?

442
00:20:54,559 --> 00:20:55,960
It used to be a mailman

443
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:57,839
named Fan who delivered it.

444
00:20:57,839 --> 00:20:59,160
I haven't seen him lately.

445
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:00,480
Did they replace him?

446
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:04,839
The mailman is missing.

447
00:21:05,119 --> 00:21:06,519
The photo studio was compromised too.

448
00:21:07,160 --> 00:21:08,920
Mainland security is closing the net fast.

449
00:21:09,079 --> 00:21:09,960
No.

450
00:21:10,079 --> 00:21:11,039
I need to lay low.

451
00:21:20,920 --> 00:21:21,519
Hey, brother.

452
00:21:22,440 --> 00:21:23,319
It's Lin.

453
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:26,400
I want to find a new place.

454
00:21:27,880 --> 00:21:29,680
My current one is leaking again.

455
00:21:32,599 --> 00:21:34,160
Help me find a better one, will you?

456
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:36,400
Thanks. Thank you.

457
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:37,400
Okay.

458
00:21:46,759 --> 00:21:47,599
She's pregnant.

459
00:21:49,240 --> 00:21:50,079
Is it her?

460
00:21:51,559 --> 00:21:52,400
Is it her?

461
00:21:52,640 --> 00:21:53,160
Is it her?

462
00:22:19,119 --> 00:22:20,559
If I'd known they were coming for you,

463
00:22:20,559 --> 00:22:22,640
I'd never have said I was in your dorm.

464
00:22:23,039 --> 00:22:24,839
I don't care if they detain me.

465
00:22:25,039 --> 00:22:26,720
But why put you on academic probation?

466
00:22:28,079 --> 00:22:28,599
Will this penalty

467
00:22:28,599 --> 00:22:29,960
go on your permanent record?

468
00:22:30,359 --> 00:22:31,079
Listen to me,

469
00:22:31,160 --> 00:22:32,440
I'll go see your homeroom teacher later.

470
00:22:32,440 --> 00:22:33,200
Slip her some money,

471
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:34,359
and this will all be sorted out.

472
00:22:34,839 --> 00:22:36,839
The one who came to see me that day was a cop.

473
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:39,279
As soon as she walked in, she told me

474
00:22:39,440 --> 00:22:40,440
she'd keep it a secret.

475
00:22:40,640 --> 00:22:41,559
But look what happened.

476
00:22:41,599 --> 00:22:43,640
You shouldn't have confessed.

477
00:22:44,079 --> 00:22:45,559
I was the one who did all those things.

478
00:22:45,559 --> 00:22:46,440
Now that you've confessed,

479
00:22:46,440 --> 00:22:47,880
what if you can't even become a teacher?

480
00:22:47,880 --> 00:22:49,039
Wouldn't your college years be for nothing?

481
00:22:49,039 --> 00:22:50,119
I might as well be dead.

482
00:22:51,039 --> 00:22:52,519
If you hadn't scrimped and saved

483
00:22:52,519 --> 00:22:53,839
to pay for my education,

484
00:22:54,319 --> 00:22:56,000
I'd probably still be back in Sichuan.

485
00:22:56,279 --> 00:22:57,119
I'd be married off

486
00:22:57,119 --> 00:22:58,799
with three kids by now.

487
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:00,759
Still out cutting grass for the pigs.

488
00:23:01,279 --> 00:23:02,160
Don't bring that up.

489
00:23:03,200 --> 00:23:04,119
Let's drop it.

490
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:08,839
Hold on tight.

491
00:23:08,839 --> 00:23:10,000
I'm taking you to eat some pig brains.

492
00:23:15,839 --> 00:23:16,480
So, what do you think?

493
00:23:16,920 --> 00:23:18,039
Nice place, isn't it?

494
00:23:18,039 --> 00:23:18,799
It's pretty good.

495
00:23:19,359 --> 00:23:21,599
Look at this beautiful big balcony of yours.

496
00:23:22,279 --> 00:23:23,960
It really pays to be the boss.

497
00:23:23,960 --> 00:23:24,920
Such a big house,

498
00:23:24,920 --> 00:23:26,039
and you just up and move.

499
00:23:26,839 --> 00:23:28,039
Life is short.

500
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:29,880
We need to treat ourselves well.

501
00:23:30,039 --> 00:23:31,200
Being miserable every day

502
00:23:31,200 --> 00:23:32,200
is such a waste.

503
00:23:34,119 --> 00:23:35,359
I don't work that hard.

504
00:23:35,599 --> 00:23:36,480
I just have a hard life.

505
00:23:39,759 --> 00:23:41,279
A close neighbor is better than a distant relative.

506
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:43,240
Who's living next door to me anyway?

507
00:23:44,920 --> 00:23:46,359
Another boss, just like you.

508
00:23:46,359 --> 00:23:48,079
Then he moved away for some reason.

509
00:23:49,279 --> 00:23:50,519
When I get some money in the future,

510
00:23:50,519 --> 00:23:51,599
I'll come be your neighbor.

511
00:23:52,559 --> 00:23:53,599
Not a problem!

512
00:23:54,440 --> 00:23:55,279
Come on, let's go.

513
00:23:59,400 --> 00:23:59,880
Let's go.

514
00:24:02,359 --> 00:24:02,920
Can you carry that alright?

515
00:24:04,960 --> 00:24:05,920
Thanks, Brother Wu.

516
00:24:06,359 --> 00:24:07,319
Take care!

517
00:24:07,319 --> 00:24:08,039
Will do!

518
00:24:08,240 --> 00:24:08,960
I'll be going now.

519
00:25:41,519 --> 00:25:42,519
See you, Sister Liu.

520
00:25:43,119 --> 00:25:43,880
Goodbye.

521
00:25:45,519 --> 00:25:46,680
Why didn't you come earlier?

522
00:25:46,680 --> 00:25:48,079
I'm almost off work.

523
00:25:48,400 --> 00:25:50,079
Who are you helping out this time?

524
00:25:50,079 --> 00:25:51,000
A friend.

525
00:25:51,200 --> 00:25:52,240
They rented out their house.

526
00:25:52,400 --> 00:25:53,680
The tenant stayed a few months and ran off.

527
00:25:53,920 --> 00:25:54,880
Please help me check.

528
00:25:55,039 --> 00:25:55,759
It'll just be a minute.

529
00:25:56,920 --> 00:25:58,559
By the way, still working at the Medical Bureau?

530
00:25:58,559 --> 00:25:59,279
Not anymore.

531
00:25:59,519 --> 00:26:00,400
I quit to start my own business.

532
00:26:00,720 --> 00:26:01,400
Good for you.

533
00:26:07,640 --> 00:26:09,400
People move around a lot in this area.

534
00:26:09,400 --> 00:26:10,240
I can't find anything.

535
00:26:10,240 --> 00:26:11,039
Forget it. Stop looking.

536
00:26:11,039 --> 00:26:12,000
I don't want to keep you after work.

537
00:26:13,640 --> 00:26:15,400
By the way, here's a face mask for you.

538
00:26:16,000 --> 00:26:16,720
It's from Hong Kong, China.

539
00:26:16,880 --> 00:26:18,279
Someone brought it back from a business trip.

540
00:26:18,720 --> 00:26:19,799
I really shouldn't.

541
00:26:19,799 --> 00:26:21,359
It's fine. I trouble you so often.

542
00:26:21,359 --> 00:26:22,079
Just take it.

543
00:26:22,359 --> 00:26:23,000
Thank you.

544
00:26:35,559 --> 00:26:38,480
Scrubbing a back is like gathering intel.

545
00:26:38,680 --> 00:26:39,839
You can't just use brute force.

546
00:26:39,839 --> 00:26:42,240
You need skill and rhythm.

547
00:26:42,680 --> 00:26:44,640
You must know when to apply pressure.

548
00:26:44,640 --> 00:26:46,319
Just focus on scrubbing.

549
00:26:46,440 --> 00:26:48,039
Enough with the theories.

550
00:26:48,960 --> 00:26:50,680
Trying to be the director, huh?

551
00:26:50,960 --> 00:26:52,359
If you're slacking off, just admit it.

552
00:26:52,920 --> 00:26:54,559
Enough with the excuses.

553
00:26:54,559 --> 00:26:57,559
You can press a little harder on the left shoulder blade, though.

554
00:26:58,599 --> 00:26:59,400
Right.

555
00:27:00,160 --> 00:27:01,880
I have been pressing hard.

556
00:27:02,599 --> 00:27:05,160
Our recent focus has been on Minzhong.

557
00:27:05,359 --> 00:27:06,559
Party, government, and military.

558
00:27:06,880 --> 00:27:09,400
Our comrades in all sectors have mobilized.

559
00:27:10,319 --> 00:27:11,799
Our near-term goal,

560
00:27:12,039 --> 00:27:13,960
aside from the updated map,

561
00:27:14,440 --> 00:27:16,279
is the mainland's military exercise movements.

562
00:27:17,640 --> 00:27:18,559
Word is,

563
00:27:18,960 --> 00:27:21,319
their navy, army, and air force are gearing up.

564
00:27:23,079 --> 00:27:23,920
"Word is."

565
00:27:24,359 --> 00:27:25,200
What I want

566
00:27:25,599 --> 00:27:28,000
are things I can see and touch.

567
00:27:28,400 --> 00:27:29,480
Yes, sir.

568
00:27:29,480 --> 00:27:31,400
We'll get the goods soon.

569
00:27:31,400 --> 00:27:33,920
We won't be slower than the Security Bureau or the military.

570
00:27:34,400 --> 00:27:35,279
Today,

571
00:27:35,720 --> 00:27:38,279
the TV news was saying

572
00:27:39,279 --> 00:27:40,720
that the Taiwan Strait

573
00:27:40,799 --> 00:27:42,000
is like a banquet.

574
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:43,400
Whoever has the longest chopsticks

575
00:27:43,640 --> 00:27:45,119
gets the most meat.

576
00:27:45,480 --> 00:27:46,400
Brother,

577
00:27:46,559 --> 00:27:47,920
you need to step it up.

578
00:27:51,440 --> 00:27:53,119
That missile lead...

579
00:27:53,119 --> 00:27:54,480
Haven't you been tracking it?

580
00:27:54,599 --> 00:27:55,440
How's it going?

581
00:27:55,799 --> 00:27:57,440
The fish is cunning.

582
00:27:57,799 --> 00:27:59,319
It took the bait a while ago.

583
00:27:59,319 --> 00:28:01,480
But it keeps swallowing it and spitting it out.

584
00:28:01,480 --> 00:28:02,359
I'll hurry.

585
00:28:02,599 --> 00:28:03,799
Hurry up.

586
00:28:05,079 --> 00:28:05,880
If I

587
00:28:06,559 --> 00:28:08,240
didn't have these old bones,

588
00:28:08,240 --> 00:28:09,640
I'd do it myself.

589
00:28:13,440 --> 00:28:15,799
The fish definitely won't get away.

590
00:28:16,759 --> 00:28:17,920
If worst comes to worst,

591
00:28:17,920 --> 00:28:19,279
I'll dive in and catch it myself.

592
00:28:52,599 --> 00:28:57,039
Comrade 92973, please record.

593
00:28:57,680 --> 00:29:00,079
1544

594
00:29:01,119 --> 00:29:03,680
4558

595
00:29:04,640 --> 00:29:06,799
4878

596
00:29:08,960 --> 00:29:13,400
Comrade 92973, please record.

597
00:29:13,920 --> 00:29:16,319
1544

598
00:29:17,359 --> 00:29:19,920
4558

599
00:29:20,880 --> 00:29:23,039
4878

600
00:29:41,440 --> 00:29:43,000
Cao Liaoping has no children

601
00:29:43,480 --> 00:29:44,680
and no attachments.

602
00:29:45,240 --> 00:29:47,200
The only person he cares about is his only nephew,

603
00:29:47,200 --> 00:29:48,200
Cao Xiao'ou.

604
00:29:49,119 --> 00:29:50,200
They've taken the stage.

605
00:29:50,519 --> 00:29:51,599
It's time for the show to begin.

606
00:29:58,079 --> 00:29:59,839
Fellow student volunteers,

607
00:30:00,279 --> 00:30:01,960
our provincial Ethnic Minority Sports Games

608
00:30:01,960 --> 00:30:03,279
are about to begin.

609
00:30:03,599 --> 00:30:06,279
Let's show our best spirit,

610
00:30:06,400 --> 00:30:09,200
because you represent the image of our city.

611
00:30:09,400 --> 00:30:10,079
Hello.

612
00:30:11,200 --> 00:30:12,200
Excuse me, I'm sorry.

613
00:30:19,240 --> 00:30:19,839
Thank you.

614
00:30:31,400 --> 00:30:34,240
Girls, keep your hands in front.

615
00:30:34,240 --> 00:30:36,680
Maintain an elegant posture.

616
00:30:37,279 --> 00:30:38,359
Clothing companies...

617
00:30:38,960 --> 00:30:40,759
Custom sportswear

618
00:30:40,920 --> 00:30:42,119
isn't handled here.

619
00:30:42,119 --> 00:30:43,160
Go out, take a right.

620
00:30:43,359 --> 00:30:44,359
Director's office.

621
00:30:44,559 --> 00:30:45,359
Chief Cao.

622
00:30:45,960 --> 00:30:47,440
I came here specifically for you.

623
00:30:47,759 --> 00:30:49,279
Your clothes and shoes

624
00:30:49,279 --> 00:30:50,599
won't even fit in my office.

625
00:30:50,880 --> 00:30:51,680
Besides,

626
00:30:51,880 --> 00:30:53,759
I can't make the call.

627
00:30:53,759 --> 00:30:54,640
You've got the wrong guy.

628
00:30:55,119 --> 00:30:56,559
I'm not here to sell things.

629
00:30:56,759 --> 00:30:58,759
I'm here to discuss corporate sponsorships.

630
00:30:59,359 --> 00:31:01,599
Like opening ceremony ads.

631
00:31:03,799 --> 00:31:04,480
Mr. Lin.

632
00:31:05,160 --> 00:31:07,119
Your timing is absolutely perfect.

633
00:31:07,319 --> 00:31:08,279
Have a seat. Come.

634
00:31:08,319 --> 00:31:09,119
Look,

635
00:31:10,640 --> 00:31:11,839
take a look at this.

636
00:31:13,480 --> 00:31:15,599
Provincial Ethnic Minority Sports Games.

637
00:31:16,039 --> 00:31:16,759
Held every four years.

638
00:31:16,759 --> 00:31:18,079
This is the third one.

639
00:31:18,559 --> 00:31:19,640
Its sporting events include

640
00:31:19,799 --> 00:31:22,440
top spinning, cuqiu, cuju,

641
00:31:22,440 --> 00:31:24,079
shuttlecock, and crossbow shooting,

642
00:31:24,079 --> 00:31:26,079
as well as ethnic martial arts.

643
00:31:26,400 --> 00:31:28,039
And when the time comes,

644
00:31:28,519 --> 00:31:29,319
the Gaoshan ethnic group

645
00:31:29,920 --> 00:31:30,880
will also participate.

646
00:31:32,400 --> 00:31:33,200
Look at this.

647
00:31:33,559 --> 00:31:34,480
What other sporting event

648
00:31:34,480 --> 00:31:36,440
has such a rich variety of games?

649
00:31:36,759 --> 00:31:38,079
They may be minorities,

650
00:31:38,079 --> 00:31:39,519
but there's nothing minor about them.

651
00:31:39,759 --> 00:31:41,640
There are a thousand athletes alone.

652
00:31:41,640 --> 00:31:42,680
This is the highest-level

653
00:31:42,680 --> 00:31:44,680
provincial competition coming up.

654
00:31:45,519 --> 00:31:46,839
Is it possible

655
00:31:47,279 --> 00:31:49,279
to organize something related to cross-strait relations?

656
00:31:49,680 --> 00:31:51,680
That way, I can easily explain it to the chamber of commerce.

657
00:31:52,279 --> 00:31:53,680
You mean

658
00:31:54,480 --> 00:31:55,880
you want to add events?

659
00:31:55,880 --> 00:31:57,880
It doesn't necessarily have to be a competition.

660
00:31:58,680 --> 00:31:59,960
Are there any local schools

661
00:31:59,960 --> 00:32:02,279
that specialize in sports?

662
00:32:02,279 --> 00:32:03,599
Like dragon boat racing.

663
00:32:03,599 --> 00:32:04,480
I remember

664
00:32:04,839 --> 00:32:07,279
there's some kind of

665
00:32:07,279 --> 00:32:08,440
football school on the southern island.

666
00:32:08,440 --> 00:32:09,759
It has quite a long history.

667
00:32:10,680 --> 00:32:11,279
Yes.

668
00:32:11,640 --> 00:32:12,640
Nankang School.

669
00:32:12,640 --> 00:32:14,160
Its centennial is coming up.

670
00:32:14,160 --> 00:32:16,000
They were founded on athletics.

671
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:17,119
Specializing in swimming.

672
00:32:17,480 --> 00:32:18,599
Are you an alumnus?

673
00:32:18,599 --> 00:32:19,759
No, no, I'm not.

674
00:32:19,880 --> 00:32:22,000
My uncle graduated from there.

675
00:32:22,839 --> 00:32:23,680
My biological uncle.

676
00:32:25,640 --> 00:32:27,119
So what can I do?

677
00:32:27,279 --> 00:32:28,319
For example,

678
00:32:28,839 --> 00:32:30,160
sponsoring anniversary gifts.

679
00:32:31,079 --> 00:32:32,920
That would be absolutely wonderful.

680
00:32:36,519 --> 00:32:37,160
Excuse me!

681
00:32:37,559 --> 00:32:38,200
Hey there!

682
00:32:40,440 --> 00:32:41,240
Over here.

683
00:32:53,359 --> 00:32:54,359
Remember me?

684
00:32:55,359 --> 00:32:57,480
International Investment Month at Yushan Hall.

685
00:32:57,880 --> 00:32:58,960
You were volunteers too.

686
00:32:58,960 --> 00:32:59,880
We've met.

687
00:33:03,440 --> 00:33:04,319
Can I help you?

688
00:33:05,480 --> 00:33:06,759
On a hot day like this,

689
00:33:06,960 --> 00:33:08,759
you didn't even buy everyone drinks?

690
00:33:09,519 --> 00:33:12,000
Do volunteers like you get paid?

691
00:33:12,519 --> 00:33:13,599
What do you want?

692
00:33:13,759 --> 00:33:14,799
We have an event coming up,

693
00:33:14,799 --> 00:33:15,759
and we'd like your help.

694
00:33:16,079 --> 00:33:16,920
We'll pay you, of course.

695
00:33:16,920 --> 00:33:18,480
Volunteers don't work for free.

696
00:33:19,519 --> 00:33:21,079
Could I get your number?

697
00:33:21,319 --> 00:33:22,119
Sure.

698
00:33:44,359 --> 00:33:45,119
Are you trying to kill me?

699
00:33:46,160 --> 00:33:48,039
I nearly died of fright just watching the car and waiting!

700
00:33:48,400 --> 00:33:49,480
I mean, you were leaning against the window.

701
00:33:49,480 --> 00:33:50,960
You could've at least said something.

702
00:33:51,079 --> 00:33:52,960
Did you know there was a guy in State Security

703
00:33:53,000 --> 00:33:54,640
who was sent to the hospital by a prank like this?

704
00:33:54,640 --> 00:33:55,519
He had a heart attack and died.

705
00:33:55,519 --> 00:33:56,519
They couldn't save him in the end.

706
00:33:56,519 --> 00:33:57,200
Did you know that?

707
00:35:01,079 --> 00:35:02,159
Attention everyone,

708
00:35:02,159 --> 00:35:04,159
Last-minute notice from the office.

709
00:35:04,159 --> 00:35:05,159
In ten minutes,

710
00:35:05,360 --> 00:35:07,760
everyone head to the third-floor conference room.

711
00:35:08,000 --> 00:35:08,800
What's the meeting about?

712
00:35:10,559 --> 00:35:11,440
Confidentiality training.

713
00:35:11,760 --> 00:35:13,480
A designated officer from the security department

714
00:35:13,480 --> 00:35:15,320
is here to give everyone a lecture.

715
00:35:16,079 --> 00:35:16,719
I'm taking leave.

716
00:35:16,719 --> 00:35:17,840
No leaves allowed.

717
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:19,840
Just say I was in a rush to get to the meeting,

718
00:35:19,840 --> 00:35:21,079
tripped while going up the stairs,

719
00:35:21,079 --> 00:35:22,239
and busted my lip.

720
00:36:45,920 --> 00:36:47,239
Inside Institute 761,

721
00:36:47,559 --> 00:36:49,039
someone is making friends with Taipei.

722
00:36:50,079 --> 00:36:51,239
How far it's gone

723
00:36:51,760 --> 00:36:52,800
isn't clear yet.

724
00:36:53,480 --> 00:36:54,440
When you go out later,

725
00:36:54,719 --> 00:36:56,639
in the second trash can on the right of the entrance,

726
00:36:57,159 --> 00:36:58,400
there's some intel for you.

727
00:36:58,599 --> 00:37:00,119
Nothing major, but nothing trivial either.

728
00:37:00,360 --> 00:37:01,639
It's enough for you to report back.

729
00:37:02,119 --> 00:37:03,119
I wouldn't be so sure.

730
00:37:03,559 --> 00:37:04,559
The people over there

731
00:37:04,920 --> 00:37:06,280
have a big appetite lately.

732
00:37:06,639 --> 00:37:08,119
They don't care about small fry.

733
00:37:08,719 --> 00:37:10,679
They want to catch a big fish.

734
00:37:15,119 --> 00:37:15,880
How big?

735
00:37:19,400 --> 00:37:20,519
As big as a missile.

736
00:37:27,800 --> 00:37:28,719
Within three days,

737
00:37:29,280 --> 00:37:30,920
I'll give you two more pieces of Class-A intel.

738
00:37:31,440 --> 00:37:32,880
And the funds will be delivered in full.

739
00:37:32,880 --> 00:37:34,559
About Institute 761,

740
00:37:34,559 --> 00:37:35,800
this is all I know.

741
00:37:36,159 --> 00:37:37,800
Things aren't moving as fast as you think.

742
00:37:38,039 --> 00:37:39,679
I'm more concerned about something else.

743
00:37:42,159 --> 00:37:43,119
Around me,

744
00:37:43,719 --> 00:37:44,599
is there anyone from their side?

745
00:37:45,119 --> 00:37:46,679
I'm working on it.

746
00:37:47,000 --> 00:37:48,320
With my status,

747
00:37:48,360 --> 00:37:51,239
it's very hard to get these things.

748
00:37:52,639 --> 00:37:53,440
No rush.

749
00:37:53,519 --> 00:37:54,440
I can wait.

750
00:38:00,639 --> 00:38:02,440
Until you use the intel I gave you

751
00:38:02,639 --> 00:38:03,800
to trade for more.

752
00:38:04,280 --> 00:38:05,000
Good luck.

753
00:38:10,480 --> 00:38:11,800
Whether this intel is real or fake,

754
00:38:11,800 --> 00:38:12,639
can't you tell?

755
00:38:12,800 --> 00:38:14,199
You've been living in peacetime for too long, huh?

756
00:38:14,559 --> 00:38:15,719
Wasting time every single day!

757
00:38:16,119 --> 00:38:16,760
Get out!

758
00:38:16,800 --> 00:38:17,440
Yes, sir.

759
00:38:19,280 --> 00:38:19,840
Old Zhang.

760
00:38:20,360 --> 00:38:20,800
Old Wei.

761
00:38:20,800 --> 00:38:21,599
How's the Director's mood?

762
00:38:22,800 --> 00:38:23,679
Wei Guangjin!

763
00:38:23,880 --> 00:38:24,800
Coming!

764
00:38:26,719 --> 00:38:27,440
Director.

765
00:38:28,519 --> 00:38:30,119
You submitted this watered-down intel?

766
00:38:31,159 --> 00:38:32,119
What's the situation in Kinmen?

767
00:38:32,400 --> 00:38:33,119
What's the situation in Kaohsiung?

768
00:38:33,119 --> 00:38:34,119
Don't you know?

769
00:38:34,320 --> 00:38:35,559
What the hell is Division Two doing?

770
00:38:35,719 --> 00:38:36,599
Was this Ma Qi's doing?

771
00:38:37,679 --> 00:38:39,719
Ma Qi got a piece of key intel

772
00:38:40,320 --> 00:38:42,159
confirming the MIB's target

773
00:38:42,519 --> 00:38:43,599
is Institute 761.

774
00:38:43,760 --> 00:38:44,639
Regarding the missiles,

775
00:38:44,840 --> 00:38:46,440
someone on our side and Taiwan, China

776
00:38:46,440 --> 00:38:47,559
have been in frequent contact.

777
00:38:48,880 --> 00:38:49,440
Sit.

778
00:38:53,840 --> 00:38:55,880
Institute 761 recently had a breakthrough

779
00:38:55,880 --> 00:38:56,639
in missile fuel.

780
00:38:57,079 --> 00:38:58,840
That's definitely what they're after.

781
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:01,119
Something big is going to happen.

782
00:39:04,280 --> 00:39:05,119
Institute 761.

783
00:39:05,400 --> 00:39:07,320
Thousands of staff. A needle in a haystack.

784
00:39:08,639 --> 00:39:09,760
Time to close the net.

785
00:39:10,360 --> 00:39:11,000
We must act fast.

786
00:39:13,159 --> 00:39:15,119
Before we catch the mole in the Bureau,

787
00:39:15,519 --> 00:39:16,760
there must be absolutely no leaks.

788
00:39:17,280 --> 00:39:17,920
Otherwise,

789
00:39:18,639 --> 00:39:20,159
we'll both lose our uniforms.

790
00:39:21,719 --> 00:39:22,360
Yes, sir.

791
00:39:34,639 --> 00:39:35,599
Xinhua News Agency reports:

792
00:39:36,280 --> 00:39:37,320
The Chinese People's Liberation Army

793
00:39:37,519 --> 00:39:39,480
will, from the 21st to the 26th,

794
00:39:39,679 --> 00:39:41,239
in the open waters of the East China Sea,

795
00:39:41,239 --> 00:39:43,840
conduct surface-to-surface missile launch exercises.

796
00:39:44,000 --> 00:39:44,719
The target area

797
00:39:44,719 --> 00:39:46,719
is centered at 26 degrees, 20 minutes north latitude

798
00:39:46,719 --> 00:39:49,039
and 122 degrees, ten minutes east longitude,

799
00:39:49,039 --> 00:39:50,960
within a circular sea area of a ten-nautical-mile radius.

800
00:39:50,960 --> 00:39:51,840
For safety reasons,

801
00:39:51,840 --> 00:39:53,840
the Chinese government asks relevant

802
00:39:53,840 --> 00:39:54,880
governments and regional authorities

803
00:39:55,119 --> 00:39:57,480
to notify their respective ships and aircraft

804
00:39:57,840 --> 00:39:58,639
that during this period,

805
00:39:58,639 --> 00:40:00,800
they must not enter the aforementioned waters and airspace.

806
00:40:13,159 --> 00:40:14,320
I thought you'd already left.

807
00:40:16,280 --> 00:40:17,519
There was some work at the archives,

808
00:40:17,519 --> 00:40:18,599
so I put in some overtime.

809
00:40:19,679 --> 00:40:21,360
Are you heading home, or...?

810
00:40:22,599 --> 00:40:24,880
If there was a bed by the road, I'd lie down.

811
00:40:25,039 --> 00:40:26,719
Where else would I go when I'm this tired?

812
00:40:28,760 --> 00:40:29,559
You must be hungry.

813
00:40:30,039 --> 00:40:31,119
Let me treat you to some Guobian.

814
00:40:31,280 --> 00:40:33,280
There's a great new place nearby.

815
00:40:35,280 --> 00:40:37,159
My ride is here. Forget it.

816
00:40:38,760 --> 00:40:40,000
Are you meeting Chunxiao?

817
00:40:44,119 --> 00:40:45,519
Do I need to report to you?

818
00:40:46,559 --> 00:40:47,920
Don't you think Chunxiao is suspicious?

819
00:40:48,239 --> 00:40:49,360
He's definitely their inside man.

820
00:41:21,119 --> 00:41:21,920
Is this the post office?

821
00:41:22,360 --> 00:41:24,440
Why can't I get through to your duty line?

822
00:41:24,679 --> 00:41:26,039
A package was misdelivered to me.

823
00:41:26,480 --> 00:41:27,840
Could you check on it for me?

824
00:41:28,960 --> 00:41:30,480
Right, over on Qinhu Road.

825
00:41:31,039 --> 00:41:31,639
Yes.

826
00:41:32,000 --> 00:41:33,960
It seems there's a new postman these past few days.

827
00:41:34,920 --> 00:41:36,400
I've been on a business trip.

828
00:41:36,400 --> 00:41:38,159
But I had a relative ask for me.

829
00:41:38,400 --> 00:41:39,599
Has anyone asked you?

830
00:41:40,599 --> 00:41:41,559
A man.

831
00:41:42,519 --> 00:41:43,519
Yes, exactly.

832
00:41:44,000 --> 00:41:45,199
When did he ask you?

833
00:41:48,039 --> 00:41:48,519
It's fine.

834
00:41:48,519 --> 00:41:49,360
As long as he asked.

835
00:41:49,400 --> 00:41:50,119
Thanks.

836
00:41:55,039 --> 00:41:55,960
For this kind of thing,

837
00:41:55,960 --> 00:41:57,840
you should go straight to your superior.

838
00:41:58,320 --> 00:41:59,800
What if I'm an accomplice?

839
00:41:59,880 --> 00:42:01,119
Aren't you afraid I'll tell him?

840
00:42:01,440 --> 00:42:02,159
You won't.

841
00:42:02,559 --> 00:42:03,320
I know what I'm doing.

842
00:42:03,320 --> 00:42:04,800
How do you know I won't?

843
00:42:05,239 --> 00:42:06,920
And how do you know he would?

844
00:42:07,440 --> 00:42:08,239
What are you trying to say?

845
00:42:09,360 --> 00:42:10,599
Objectively speaking,

846
00:42:10,719 --> 00:42:11,880
if I were him,

847
00:42:11,880 --> 00:42:13,199
and if I were really compromised,

848
00:42:13,559 --> 00:42:15,480
would I leave that little notebook in the office?

849
00:42:16,320 --> 00:42:17,599
Besides, the things he recorded in it...

850
00:42:17,599 --> 00:42:18,639
That's your opinion.

851
00:42:19,159 --> 00:42:20,119
It's not my opinion.

852
00:42:22,679 --> 00:42:24,280
You just don't want him to be the mole.

853
00:42:24,800 --> 00:42:25,400
Right?

854
00:42:29,119 --> 00:42:30,599
In my very first class here,

855
00:42:30,599 --> 00:42:31,960
I heard a saying.

856
00:42:33,000 --> 00:42:35,199
We shouldn't suspect our comrades without reason.

857
00:42:35,360 --> 00:42:36,480
We are not the Zhongtong.

858
00:42:36,599 --> 00:42:38,800
Whether Chunxiao is compromised and what I want...

859
00:42:38,800 --> 00:42:39,800
are two different things.

860
00:42:40,079 --> 00:42:40,960
If you think he's compromised,

861
00:42:40,960 --> 00:42:42,320
just bring out the evidence.

862
00:42:42,320 --> 00:42:43,199
I will, very soon.

863
00:42:43,559 --> 00:42:44,960
Don't think I'm just jealous of him.

864
00:42:45,159 --> 00:42:46,639
Professional sensitivity and political awareness,

865
00:42:46,880 --> 00:42:47,599
I do have those.

866
00:42:54,119 --> 00:42:54,800
Move to the back.

867
00:42:54,800 --> 00:42:55,960
There are seats in the back!

868
00:43:08,360 --> 00:43:09,079
I'm Wang Kai,

869
00:43:09,440 --> 00:43:10,800
inviting you to watch the drama

870
00:43:11,079 --> 00:43:11,800
Confrontation.

871
00:43:12,039 --> 00:43:13,599
Are you quitting just for today,

872
00:43:13,840 --> 00:43:15,480
or are you quitting for good?

873
00:43:15,519 --> 00:43:17,840
It makes no difference to me.

874
00:43:17,840 --> 00:43:19,320
Cao Liaoping is done for good.

875
00:43:20,280 --> 00:43:21,440
Boss Lin, you can't leave.

876
00:43:21,519 --> 00:43:22,440
I told you I have an emergency.

877
00:43:22,440 --> 00:43:23,039
I won't short you on the money.

878
00:43:23,039 --> 00:43:24,960
Boss Lin, a big boss like you can't leave without paying.

879
00:43:25,440 --> 00:43:26,480
Leave your watch here as collateral.

880
00:43:26,639 --> 00:43:28,119
A while ago, there was someone else

881
00:43:28,360 --> 00:43:30,079
who took an interest in this postman's movements.

882
00:43:30,159 --> 00:43:32,159
I'm almost certain it was Lin Kanshan.

883
00:43:33,960 --> 00:43:34,800
Under no circumstances

884
00:43:35,119 --> 00:43:37,599
should you do anything "at all costs."

